## 2. APK Modification / Static Patching

### Method A: Modify Network Security Config
```xml
<!-- res/xml/network_security_config.xml -->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <!-- Trust user-installed certificates -->
            <certificates src="user"/>
            <certificates src="system"/>
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
    <!-- Remove all domain-config with pin-set -->
    <domain-config>
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">target.com</domain>
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="user"/>
            <certificates src="system"/>
        </trust-anchors>
        <!-- Remove <pin-set> elements -->
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
```

### Method B: Decompile and Patch with APKTool
```bash
# Decompile APK
apktool d target.apk -o target_decompiled

# Modify smali code - find and patch certificate validation
# Look for these patterns in smali files:
grep -r "checkServerTrusted" target_decompiled/
grep -r "CertificatePinner" target_decompiled/
grep -r "pin-set" target_decompiled/

# Recompile
apktool b target_decompiled -o target_patched.apk

# Sign the APK
keytool -genkey -v -keystore test.keystore -alias test -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
jarsigner -verbose -sigalg SHA1withRSA -digestalg SHA1 -keystore test.keystore target_patched.apk test

# Align
zipalign -v 4 target_patched.apk target_final.apk
```

